        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospital admission of your 83-year-old female patient, who presented with an acute exacerbation of her known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, she exhibited increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Diagnostic workup included chest X-ray confirming hyperinflation, arterial blood gas analysis revealing hypoxaemia, and blood tests showing mild inflammatory markers. Pulse oximetry was monitored continuously throughout her stay. She was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, supplemental oxygen therapy, and supportive intravenous fluids. She responded well to treatment with significant symptomatic improvement. Prior to discharge, patient education regarding inhaler technique and exacerbation management was provided. We recommend close outpatient follow-up and review of her maintenance inhaler regimen. Please do not hesitate to contact us should you require further information.</div>"
            },
            "code": {
